      en: "The Major Bell Tower is a historic bell tower in Maseru, built in 1907 in honor of Major James Bell, a British colonial official. The tower is 18 meters high and built of sandstone. It originally served as a watchtower and bell tower for the nearby Anglican church. During colonial times it was used as a lookout point to monitor the border with South Africa. Today it is a protected monument and a city landmark.",
