      en: "Mofoka Village is a living museum of Basotho culture, located in the Senqu Valley. The village is surrounded by terraced fields. Each homestead consists of several huts, painted with geometric patterns. The villagers practice subsistence farming. They also produce handcrafted pottery and baskets. The village has a community guesthouse for tourists.",
